<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;DONBASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Donbass is a region where events took place, particularly during the War in Donbass and involving various military divisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAR IN DONBASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The War in Donbass is a conflict that led to the renaming of military divisions with the King Danylo honorific."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REVOLUTIONARY MILITARY COUNCIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Revolutionary Military Council ordered the formation of the 1st Simbirsk Infantry Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1ST SIMBIRSK INFANTRY DIVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1st Simbirsk Infantry Division was formed in 1918 and later renamed as the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;24TH SIMBIRSK RIFLE DIVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"24th Simbirsk Rifle Division actively participated in the Russian Civil War and was involved in various regions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUSSIAN CIVIL WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Russian Civil War is the conflict in which the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division participated, affecting its operations and movements."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAKSIM PURKAYEV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maksim Purkayev was a future Army General and a regimental commander of the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;70TH MOTOR RIFLE REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"70th Motor Rifle Regiment is one of the units that formed part of the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;71ST MOTOR RIFLE REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"71st Motor Rifle Regiment is one of the units that formed part of the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;72ND MOTOR RIFLE REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"72nd Motor Rifle Regiment is one of the units that formed part of the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;392ND TANK REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"392nd Tank Regiment is one of the units that formed part of the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;50TH GUARDS TRAINING ARTILLERY REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"50th Guards Training Artillery Regiment is one of the units that formed part of the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1203RD ANTI-AIRCRAFT MISSILE REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1203rd Anti-aircraft Missile Regiment is one of the units that formed part of the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;42ND GUARDS MRD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"42nd Guards MRD is a unit that existed after World War II and later became the 173 Guards District Training Centre."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;173 GUARDS DISTRICT TRAINING CENTRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"173 Guards District Training Centre is a training centre that existed from 1987 to 1992 and comprised several motor rifle regiments, a tank regiment, a guards training artillery regiment, and an air-defense regiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHECHENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chechens are mentioned as receiving some of the weapons from the 173 Guards Training Centre during its disbandment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;4 JANUARY 1992&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"4 January 1992 is the date when the 173 Guards District Training Centre was disbanded."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECOND CHECHEN WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Second Chechen War is an event that occurred after the disbandment of the 173 Guards District Training Centre."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROZNY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grozny is a city where the 42nd Guards MRD was located in 1957."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHALI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shali is a location where the 392nd Tank Regiment was stationed in 1991."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Holm is mentioned as a source for information about the 173 Guards Training Centre."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;12TH ARMY CORPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"12th Army Corps is the parent organization of the 173 Guards District Training Centre."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;1ST SIMBIRSK INFANTRY DIVISION&quot;" target="&quot;24TH SIMBIRSK RIFLE DIVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"1st Simbirsk Infantry Division was renamed to 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division following the War in Donbass."</data>
      <data key="d5">"renaming, historical context"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;24TH SIMBIRSK RIFLE DIVISION&quot;" target="&quot;RUSSIAN CIVIL WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"24th Simbirsk Rifle Division actively participated in the Russian Civil War, affecting its operations and movements."</data>
      <data key="d5">"participation, conflict"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
